# What the thread sanitizer reports that is not a race of the program's.
#
# A block the system disposes of on a thread of its own, after it has run
# it: libdispatch reaches the block's dispose helper through calls of its
# own, which the sanitizer does not intercept, so the order the system
# keeps between the program's thread and that one is not seen. The dispose
# helper's count is atomic; what came before it on the program's thread is
# reported as unordered with it.
race:_call_dispose_helpers_excp
